          "explanation": "This approach represents the professional intelligence standard for celestial verification. Astrometric plate solving can determine the exact portion of the sky visible in the image, immediately confirming or refuting the claimed latitude. The lunar phase provides precise date verification, as the moon's appearance changes daily. Security lighting shadows, even at night, can be measured to determine the sun's position below the horizon, which varies by location and time. By integrating these three independent celestial indicators, you can establish both location and timing with high confidence. This approach is superior because: (1) it uses multiple independent celestial references, (2) it doesn't rely on architectural features that might be ambiguous, (3) it doesn't depend on background details that might not be visible, and (4) it doesn't rely on metadata that could be easily manipulated.",
